Package: md2docx
Architecture: all
Depends:
 pandoc,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
Recommends:
 python3-yaml,
Description: convert Markdown to .docx driven by a configuration file
 md2docx wraps pandoc, but instead of accepting pandoc's default look it
 compiles a configuration file into two throwaway artifacts and hands them
 to pandoc: a reference.docx whose styles.xml carries the configured run
 and paragraph properties, and a Lua filter that routes inline constructs
 pandoc would otherwise render with direct formatting (emphasis, strong,
 strikeout, ...) through named character styles, so the configuration can
 reach them.
 .
 Only the Python standard library is required; python3-yaml is used when
 present so that YAML configuration files work too.
